{
  "title": "Move mana auto-handling out of GAME_PLAY_MANA callbacks",
  "description": "The bridge still executes mana-payment decisions directly on the callback thread, even though the intended model is that decisions happen synchronously when the player has priority.\n\nCurrent behavior in `Mage.Client.Bridge/src/main/java/mage/client/bridge/BridgeCallbackHandler.java`:\n- The callback switch for `GAME_PLAY_MANA` / `GAME_PLAY_XMANA` immediately calls `handleGamePlayManaAuto()` around lines 5200-5218.\n- `handleGamePlayManaAuto()` around lines 5916-6068 updates `lastGameView`, consumes `manaPlan`, updates `manaPlanAbilityIndex`, taps mana sources, spends pool mana, and can cancel the spell.\n- Only if that whole auto-handler returns false does the bridge fall back to `storePendingAction()`.\n\nWhy this is a bug:\n- Mana payment is still a decision-time side effect happening asynchronously on the callback thread.\n- `lastGameView` is mutated before the action is normalized into the synchronous pending-action flow.\n- This keeps a large amount of strategic and sequencing logic outside the newer deterministic decision-boundary pipeline.\n\nSuggested fix:\n- Make MCP-mode `GAME_PLAY_MANA` / `GAME_PLAY_XMANA` store a pending action first.\n- Run the existing mana-plan, auto-tap, pool-mana, and cancel logic from the synchronous decision-boundary path instead of from the callback handler.\n- Keep the callback-time code limited to recording the authoritative action payload and waking the waiting player thread.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "bridge",
    "mcp",
    "determinism",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-03-20T17:25:15.945300-07:00",
